{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/943174-i-don-t-get-werewolf-the-forsaken","id":943174,"title":"I don't get Werewolf the Forsaken.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-03T17:59:26-07:00","id":943174,"title":"I don't get Werewolf the Forsaken.","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"> <span style=\"color:#222222\"> I have read through the first few chapters of the 2nd edition book, and I still don't understand what makes the Uratha forsaken. They have Luna's blessing, and have since prehistory after they took up the role of father wolf. So they aren't Forsaken anymore right?<br /> Another question I have is about the Influence trait that spirits have. It seems to have limitless potential within its narrow focus, but it didn't mention rules for attacking with it. What if a storm spirit used its influence to send down a bolt of lightning to attack, is this what was intended? I am asking for balance reasons, because I want storyteller characters that are fairly balanced, but also the option for players to play as spirits in a future game.<br /> Some other things are confusing too. I have read CofD core, BtP, and VtR, but WtF seems to be the most complex, with three to four different gifts, unclear (at least to me) rules for stating out Ghost Wolves, and a few little things.<br /> I am actually using the conflict between a Ghost Wolf, and a spirit as the main story of my core CofD game. I am aware that I don't really need to use all the rules, but I'm a rules guy. Any advice is appreciated.<br /> <br /> </span><br /> <br /> </span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T18:58:28-07:00","id":943245,"title":"","content":"They are Forsaken because they butchered Luna's babydaddy. This pissed her off so much she created the Gauntlet in a fit of cosmic rage.<br /> <br /> Influence, in my opinion, is more of a subtle magic; for more 'flashy' effects, Numina are where you need to look.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T19:12:25-07:00","id":943262,"title":"","content":"They killed their father and god and in doing so destroyed the only place they can truly be home.<br /> <br /> Yes, Influence has potentially infinite potential. But for direct attacks you're more likely to use Numina. It's not a hard and fast rule but Influence is more for 'storytelling' powers and Numina for action powers.<br /> <br /> What issues are you having with Gifts and Ghost Wolves? They've likely been asked and answered before, we shouldn't have a problem helping you clear up any problems you're having for the rules.<br /> <br /> Ghost Wolves start with one less Renown than Forsaken, as you gain a Renown for joining a Tribe and the Ghost Wolves didn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-03-2016, 10:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T19:16:22-07:00","id":943267,"title":"","content":"The Forsaken are such because they murdered their parent and in doing so fucked up the world so hard that it was fundamentally changed on a cosmic level, creating the Gauntlet and severing the Shadow from the rest of the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T19:18:06-07:00","id":943270,"title":"","content":"In 1e, they heavily implied Luna, in a fit of Rage, raised the Gauntlet HERSELF, to punish werewolves. Was this changed, in 2e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T19:23:11-07:00","id":943274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/943174-i-don-t-get-werewolf-the-forsaken?p=943262#post943262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They killed their father and god and in doing so destroyed the only place they can truly be home.<br /> <br /> Yes, Influence has potentially infinite potential. But for direct attacks you're more likely to use Numina. It's not a hard and fast rule but Influence is more for 'storytelling' powers and Numina for action powers.<br /> <br /> What issues are you having with Gifts and Ghost Wolves? They've likely been asked and answered before, we shouldn't have a problem helping you clear up any problems you're having for the rules.<br /> <br /> Ghost Wolves start with one less Renown than Forsaken, as you gain a Renown for joining a Tribe and the Ghost Wolves didn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way it was worded in general, mentioning facets, wolf gifts, shadow gifts, hunter aspects, and I guess Moon powers? I have trouble keeping it all straight, and so far I think the Ghost Wolves only get two dots in their moon auspice gift thing, while the others also get a shadow gift, or get to put a point into wolf gift. The way its written makes it hard for me to interpret exactly how much a Ghost Wolf is supposed to have.<br /> <br /> Another problem I have is finding mechanics for Hunter Aspects. I see that it has a short description, but no rules to manage them. The Ithear (Cressant Moon) one dosent have rules, just aparently a story based effect.<br /> <br /> As for them being forsaken, I thought Luna supported them now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T19:23:37-07:00","id":943275,"title":"","content":"There's a number of thematic elements that cast Uratha as Forsaken:<br /> <br /> They're Forsaken because they cannot feasible live normal human lives without the not uncertain chance of getting triggered and butchering every person in the neighborhood - including your family, your friends, more than likely? Your Flesh Touchstone. They're Forsaken because the spirit-wilds hate them like you'd hate a police state. Like the gazelle would fuck with the lions if it could. They're Forsaken because, by the standards of the self-styled Pure, they're just slave to a crazy bitch of a mother that treats you like a dog instead of the predator you were born to be - and despite every proof of this, they still choose to bend knee. And for that, they'll burn, like the heretics that they are.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T19:25:27-07:00","id":943277,"title":"","content":"The Pure came from Luna right? So they don't also revere her?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T19:25:56-07:00","id":943278,"title":"","content":"In first edition Father Wolf called down the Gauntlet with his final howl to continue his duty of keeping the spirit and flesh worlds separate. It was implied that Luna cursed the Uratha with the bane of silver.<br /> <br /> In second edition, the death of Father Wolf caused the collapse of Pangaea, which left the empty Gauntlet in its absence. And Luna did not curse the Uratha with the bane of silver, though the Pure still believe she did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T19:26:34-07:00","id":943279,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/943174-i-don-t-get-werewolf-the-forsaken?p=943270#post943270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 1e, they heavily implied Luna, in a fit of Rage, raised the Gauntlet HERSELF, to punish werewolves. Was this changed, in 2e?</div> </div> </div> </div>Urfarah (Father Wolf) did, with his death howl. He was, after all, the Lord of the Border Marches. Brush up on the Ancient History chapter in the 1e corebook for confirmation</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T19:28:40-07:00","id":943283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/943174-i-don-t-get-werewolf-the-forsaken?p=943279#post943279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> Urfarah (Father Wolf) did, with his death howl. He was, after all, the Lord of the Border Marches. Brush up on the Ancient History chapter in the 1e corebook for confirmation</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Ah! Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T19:29:00-07:00","id":943284,"title":"","content":"The first addition seems to make more sense. Silver is a moon thing right, so it should come from Luna. The Gauntlet makes perfect sense if Father Wolf caused it, what caused it in second edition? I kind of wonder if I might be better off ignoring the story entirley, but it seems like a big part of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T19:32:18-07:00","id":943286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/943174-i-don-t-get-werewolf-the-forsaken?p=943270#post943270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 1e, they heavily implied Luna, in a fit of Rage, raised the Gauntlet HERSELF, to punish werewolves. Was this changed, in 2e?</div> </div> </div> </div>When reading about the Pure it said they don't have to worry about the guantlet. They are in both the shadow and the regular world at the same time as far as I understand it. So I guess Luna only punished the Uratha, not the Pure?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T19:46:12-07:00","id":943302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/943174-i-don-t-get-werewolf-the-forsaken?p=943277#post943277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Pure came from Luna right? So they don't also revere her?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Pure loathe Luna and carve the Auspices she grants out of their flesh in horrifically painful rites to prove it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T19:48:29-07:00","id":943307,"title":"","content":"Why do they hate their mother?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T19:50:08-07:00","id":943310,"title":"","content":"Alright I think I got this all. I took a nasty fall earlier and wonked y head pretty bad but if I got something wrong I'm sure someone will pipe up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The way it was worded in general, mentioning facets, wolf gifts, shadow gifts, hunter aspects, and I guess Moon powers? I have trouble keeping it all straight, and so far I think the Ghost Wolves only get two dots in their moon auspice gift thing, while the others also get a shadow gift, or get to put a point into wolf gift. The way its written makes it hard for me to interpret exactly how much a Ghost Wolf is supposed to have. </div> </div> </div>Three kinds of gifts. Moon Gifts, which range in power from 1-5 and are granted via your Auspice, thus Luna and lunes. Shadow Gifts, which are all relatively the same power and are taken from spirits. And Wolf Gifts, which are more of an enhancement of your supernatural abilities and can be grown without assistance. Wolf Gifts are kind of like 'super merits.'<br /> <br /> A Ghost Wolf puts 1 Renown into its Auspice upon creation. Doing so it gets one Moon Gift. Then it gets another dot of Renown it can put anywhere. If it puts it in its Auspice Renown it gets two Moon Gifts. Otherwise it gets an Shadow Gift facet with the associated Renown. Then it gets a Wolf Gift.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Another problem I have is finding mechanics for Hunter Aspects. I see that it has a short description, but no rules to manage them. The Ithear (Cressant Moon) one dosent have rules, just aparently a story based effect. </div> </div> </div>They're on page 98. If successful, they put a Condition on the target. An Ithaeur puts the Mystified Condition on the target, detailed on p309. On humans it offers a penalty to all Mental Rolls based on the Gauntlet Rating.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for them being forsaken, I thought Luna supported them now? </div> </div> </div>She forgave them. That didn't bring Father Wolf or Pangaea back.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Pure came from Luna right? So they don't also revere her? </div> </div> </div>Some radicals may believe they came from a source other than Luna. But most Pure believe Luna tricked the Forsaken into killing Father Wolf and destroying Pangaea, while the Pure believe they took no part in it. They further believe she cursed them with the bane of silver. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When reading about the Pure it said they don't have to worry about the guantlet. They are in both the shadow and the regular world at the same time as far as I understand it. So I guess Luna only punished the Uratha, not the Pure? </div> </div> </div>No, the Pure have to live with the Gauntlet too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-03-2016, 10:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"