ailed on p309. On humans it offers a penalty to all Mental Rolls based on the Gauntlet Rating.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> She forgave them. That didn't bring Father Wolf or Pangaea back.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Some radicals may believe they came from a source other than Luna. But most Pure believe Luna tricked the Forsaken into killing Father Wolf and destroying Pangaea, while the Pure believe they took no part in it. They further believe she cursed them with the bane of silver.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> No, the Pure have to live with the Gauntlet too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thankyou, that was a lot, but helpful. So to clarify, you get a wolf gift no matter what in character creation right? You cant use it to get a shadow/moon gift?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T20:26:15-07:00","id":943339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/943174-i-don-t-get-werewolf-the-forsaken?p=943332#post943332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So to clarify, you get a wolf gift no matter what in character creation right? You cant use it to get a shadow/moon gift?</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't sound right. I think you only get a Wolf Gift if you didn't get two Moon Gifts for having two dots in your Auspice Renown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T20:35:49-07:00","id":943347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/943174-i-don-t-get-werewolf-the-forsaken?p=943339#post943339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That doesn't sound right. I think you only get a Wolf Gift if you didn't get two Moon Gifts for having two dots in your Auspice Renown.</div> </div> </div> </div>So... Moon gifts and shadow gifts are interchangeble, but wolf gifts arent? You have 2 dots. One has to be in your moon gift, you can put the second there too, or instead put it in a shadow gift, or a wolf gift?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T20:56:24-07:00","id":943362,"title":"","content":"When I said Golf Gifts are more like 'super merits,' I wasn't just referring to their power, they're also very cheap, at 1 Experience. Moon and Shadow Gifts, however, cost the same, 2.<br /> <br /> Oh I see what I missed. As a Ghost Wolf you start with two dots of Renown. One in your Auspice, one anywhere else. You can't start with two dots in your Auspice Renown.<br /> <br /> You get a Gift with each dot of Renown. So one Gift for your Auspice, one anywhere that matches the other Renown, and a Wolf Gift.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T21:32:43-07:00","id":943380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/943174-i-don-t-get-werewolf-the-forsaken?p=943284#post943284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first addition seems to make more sense. Silver is a moon thing right, so it should come from Luna. The Gauntlet makes perfect sense if Father Wolf caused it, what caused it in second edition? I kind of wonder if I might be better off ignoring the story entirley, but it seems like a big part of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most modern werewolves agree since silver is associated with the moon, Luna seems a likely source of their silver Bane. Similarly, most modern werewolves agree that it makes perfect sense that Fater Wolf's death howl would have been what caused the Gauntlet. As such, the prevailing version of the werewolves' origin myth among modern werewolves is that when the First Pack killed Father Wolf, his death howl created the gauntlet and Luna cursed them with the Bane of silver as punishment for their patricidal act. We, as players with access to information the characters don't have, can read the &quot;Sundered World&quot; chapter of Dark Eras and see that, in an era that predates the death of Father Wolf, werewolves already had the bane of silver, something not entirely dissimilar from the gauntlet existed in human settlements, and various factions of werewolves from generations after the First Pack had many different ideas of what to do about Urfarah's waning power, including at least one group with notions about constructing some sort of barrier in Pangaea. Where did the silver Bane really come from? Who really killed Father Wolf? What really caused the fall of Pangea and the rise of the Gauntlet? Those are mysteries for the Storyteller to decide the answer to. Or not, as it's unlikely to come up in an actual game anyway.<br /> <br /> The thing about Chronicles of Darkness is that it never gives any hard answers, at least not without those answers raising twice as many new questions. The origin myth hasn't significantly changed since 1st edition, but Dark Eras, not Werewolf 2e as a whole, has given us a glimpse into some of the truth behind the myth. In typical CofD fashion, that truth has only served to further obfuscate issues that were formerly thought to be clearly understood. I consider that a good thing, but if you don't, there's really no reason to take the Sundered World Era as absolute truth. It could just be one more version of the myth. Or it might not exist in your game at all. It's up to you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/943174-i-don-t-get-werewolf-the-forsaken?p=943286#post943286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When reading about the Pure it said they don't have to worry about the guantlet. They are in both the shadow and the regular world at the same time as far as I understand it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure where you got this impression... The Pure use the same mechanics for crossing the Gauntlet as the Forsaken do. Many of them, particularly the Firetouched, have a generally more positive relationship with most spirits than the Forsaken do, but they still have to reach at Loci just like any other werewolves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/943174-i-don-t-get-werewolf-the-forsaken?p=943286#post943286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I guess Luna only punished the Uratha, not the Pure?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, according to the myths, she punished all werewolves. That's why all werewolves are harmed by silver, that's the punishment she (allegedly) gave them. Some unspecified amount of time afterwards, a subset of werewolves made partial amends to Luna by taking the Oath of the Moon. They vowed to follow certain dictates she laid down, and in exchange she granted them Auspices and Moon Gifts, and lessened the sting of silver, but did not completely remove it. Another subset rejected the idea of cowtowing to a mother who cursed every werewolf equally, when some of them didn't participate in the murder of Father Wolf, and even actively opposed the idea. So they refused to take the Oath, and ripped the Auspices from their own souls. They are harmed even more by silver than other werewolves.<br /> <br /> In Sundered World, we see that even before Father Wolf's death, all werewolves already had Auspices, Moon Gifts, and the lessened version of the silver Bane. Removing the Auspice made the Bane worse. Again, why? We don't know. But it also has pretty minimal relevance to most Forsaken games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/943174-i-don-t-get-werewolf-the-forsaken?p=943307#post943307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do they hate their mother?</div> </div> </div> </div>As stated above, they hate her because they believe she gave them an equal share in the curse she placed on their siblings for slaying their father, when they took no part in the act and even tried to stop it. They're probably wrong, but since no one is alive who remembers what really happened, it makes little difference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T21:46:26-07:00","id":943391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/943174-i-don-t-get-werewolf-the-forsaken?p=943380#post943380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most modern werewolves agree since silver is associated with the moon, Luna seems a likely source of their silver Bane. Similarly, most modern werewolves agree that it makes perfect sense that Fater Wolf's death howl would have been what caused the Gauntlet. As such, the prevailing version of the werewolves' origin myth among modern werewolves is that when the First Pack killed Father Wolf, his death howl created the gauntlet and Luna cursed them with the Bane of silver as punishment for their patricidal act. We, as players with access to information the characters don't have, can read the &amp;quot;Sundered World&amp;quot; chapter of Dark Eras and see that, in an era that predates the death of Father Wolf, werewolves already had the bane of silver, something not entirely dissimilar from the gauntlet existed in human settlements, and various factions of werewolves from generations after the First Pack had many different ideas of what to do about Urfarah's waning power, including at least one group with notions about constructing some sort of barrier in Pangaea. Where did the silver Bane really come from? Who really killed Father Wolf? What really caused the fall of Pangea and the rise of the Gauntlet? Those are mysteries for the Storyteller to decide the answer to. Or not, as it's unlikely to come up in an actual game anyway.<br /> <br /> The thing about Chronicles of Darkness is that it never gives any hard answers, at least not without those answers raising twice as many new questions. The origin myth hasn't significantly changed since 1st edition, but Dark Eras, not Werewolf 2e as a whole, has given us a glimpse into some of the truth behind the myth. In typical CofD fashion, that truth has only served to further obfuscate issues that were formerly thought to be clearly understood. I consider that a good thing, but if you don't, there's really no reason to take the Sundered World Era as absolute truth. It could just be one more version of the myth. Or it might not exist in your game at all. It's up to you.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not sure where you got this impression... The Pure use the same mechanics for crossing the Gauntlet as the Forsaken do. Many of them, particularly the Firetouched, have a generally more positive relationship with most spirits than the Forsaken do, but they still have to reach at Loci just like any other werewolves.<br /> <br /> <br /> Well, according to the myths, she punished all werewolves. That's why all werewolves are harmed by silver, that's the punishment she (allegedly) gave them. Some unspecified amount of time afterwards, a subset of werewolves made partial amends to Luna by taking the Oath of the Moon. They vowed to follow certain dictates she laid down, and in exchange she granted them Auspices and Moon Gifts, and lessened the sting of silver, but did not completely remove it. Another subset rejected the idea of cowtowing to a mother who cursed every werewolf equally, when some of them didn't participate in the murder of Father Wolf, and even actively opposed the idea. So they refused to take the Oath, and ripped the Auspices from their own souls. They are harmed even more by silver than other werewolves.<br /> <br /> In Sundered World, we see that even before Father Wolf's death, all werewolves already had Auspices, Moon Gifts, and the lessened version of the silver Bane. Removing the Auspice made the Bane worse. Again, why? We don't know. But it also has pretty minimal relevance to most Forsaken games.<br /> <br /> <br /> As stated above, they hate her because they believe she gave them an equal share in the curse she placed on their siblings for slaying their father, when they took no part in the act and even tried to stop it. They're probably wrong, but since no one is alive who remembers what really happened, it makes little difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank-you, best summery so far. I just wanted the myth to make some since to me. Whether it's true is less important. But since the moon spirit and the lunes still interact to some degree with Uratha, I figured I better understand the story. <br /> <br /> As for the pure, in the prey chapter it said the pure have no problem breaking the rules of the shadow, and I could have sworn it mentioned the gauntlet was cursed for the forsaken, but not affecting the pure that way, but that part was in the chapter with wolf gifts I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T21:52:46-07:00","id":943394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/943174-i-don-t-get-werewolf-the-forsaken?p=943362#post943362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I said Golf Gifts are more like 'super merits,' I wasn't just referring to their power, they're also very cheap, at 1 Experience. Moon and Shadow Gifts, however, cost the same, 2.<br /> <br /> Oh I see what I missed. As a Ghost Wolf you start with two dots of Renown. One in your Auspice, one anywhere else. You can't start with two dots in your Auspice Renown.<br /> <br /> You get a Gift with each dot of Renown. So one Gift for your Auspice, one anywhere that matches the other Renown, and a Wolf Gift.</div> </div> </div> </div>But if your a Ghost Wolf you don't have a tribe so you have to put the other renown in your auspice right? Like if I had a Ghost Wolf ithaer I only get wisdom right? Can't get Cunning or Honor or something can I? Sorry I'm so confused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T21:56:50-07:00","id":943397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/943174-i-don-t-get-werewolf-the-forsaken?p=943391#post943391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the pure, in the prey chapter it said the pure have no problem breaking the rules of the shadow,</div> </div> </div> </div>The Fire-Touched are a Tribe of Pure that place an emphasis on embracing the Shadow. 'Those who would hunt the Fire-Touched must deal with their incredible armory of rites and esoteric Shadow lore - the high priests and templars of the tribe can warp the Shadow and break its laws with ease.' It's because they have powerful magics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> B<span style=\"font-family:inherit\">ut if your a Ghost Wolf you don't have a tribe so you have to put the other renown in your auspice right? Like if I had a Ghost Wolf ithaer I only get wisdom right? Can't get Cunning or Honor or something can I? Sorry I'm so confused.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">No. Two Renown dots out of character creation. One you put in your Auspice Renown. The other you put somewhere else. If you're an Ithaeur, you put your first dot in Wisdom. You put your second Renown dot in anything but Wisdom.<br /> <br /> It's no problem, hope we can get you situated.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-04-2016, 01:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T21:58:34-07:00","id":943399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/943174-i-don-t-get-werewolf-the-forsaken?p=943397#post943397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Fire-Touched are a Tribe of Pure that place an emphasis on embracing the Shadow. 'Those who would hunt the Fire-Touched must deal with their incredible armory of rites and esoteric Shadow lore - the high priests and templars of the tribe can warp the Shadow and break its laws with ease.' It's because they have powerful magics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I get it now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T22:41:40-07:00","id":943422,"title":"","content":"Ok, gonna try to break down Gifts now. There are three types of Gifts, though two of them function similarly enough that you could kind of think of it as one-and-a-half types.<br /> <br /> The first type is Moon Gifts. Moon Gifts are rated from 1 to 5 dots, and are associated with an Auspice. You automatically get one Moon Gift at character creation, at a dot rating equal to your starting dots in your Auspice's Primary Renown, and can buy additional Moon Gifts associated with your Auspice (which start at one dot when you buy them) for 5 experiences each. There is currently only one Moon Gift per Auspice, but the rule for buying more was included so that if they print additional Moon Gifts in later books they can slot right in with the existing mechanics. Any time you gain a dot in your Auspice's Primary Renown, you get one free dot in one of your Moon Gifts. Since there is currently only one Moon Gift for each Auspice, your Moon Gift should always have the same dot rating as your Auspice's primary Renown. If and when they add more Moon Gifts in the futute, you'll be able to buy dots in them for 2 experiences each, but you can never have more dots in any Moon Gift than you have in your Auspice Primary Renown.<br /> <br /> The second type is Shadow Gifts. They do not have a dot rating, but each has five powers called Facets under its umbrella, one Facet associated with each of the five Renown. Shadow Gifts can be bought for 5 experiences each, or 3 experiences if they are one of the Affinity Gifts for your Auspice or Tribe (you can think of this like the difference between in-Clan and out-of-Clan Disciplines in Requiem.) When you buy a new Gift, you get one free Facet of that Gift, which must be associated with a Renown you have at least one dot in. You can buy additional Facets in Shadow Gifts for 2 experiences each, but you cannot buy Facets associated with any Renown you don't have at least one dot in.!Any time you gain a dot in any Renown, you gain a free Facet associated with that Renown in any Shadow Gift you know. This free Facet can be banked and saved for later if (and only if) you already have the Facet associated with that Renown in all of your known Shadow Gifts.<br /> <br /> The third (or second-and-a-half) type is Wolf Gifts. Wolf Gifts work identically to Shadow Gifts, except that you are automatically considered to &quot;know&quot; all Wolf Gifts (but Facets still have to be bought with Experiences or granted when you gain Renown), and the Facets for Wolf Gifts only cost 1 experience each.<br /> <br /> At character creation, you get one free dot in your Auspice's Primary Renown, one free dot in your Tribe's Primary Renown, and one free dot in any Renown of your choice, but you cannot have three dots in any one Renown (so if your Auspex and your Tribe have the same Primary Renown, you can't put your third free dot in it as well). Since Ghost Wolves don't have a Tribe, they only get one dot in their Auspice's Primary Renown and one dot in any Renown. As per the rules for Moon Gifts, you get one Moon Gift at character creation with dots equal to your dots in your Auspice's Primary Renown. If you only have 1 dot in your Moon Gift, you also get 1 Facet of a Wolf Gift, which must be associated with a Renown you have at least one dot in. Finally, you get two free Shadow Gifts, which must both be from Gifts on your Auspice's or your Tribe's Affinity Gifts list. As per the rules for Shadow Gifts, you get one free Facet of each of these Gifts, which must be associated with a Renown you have at least one dot in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T23:46:35-07:00","id":943455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/943174-i-don-t-get-werewolf-the-forsaken?p=943422#post943422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At character creation, you get one free dot in your Auspice's Primary Renown, one free dot in your Tribe's Primary Renown, and one free dot in any Renown of your choice, but you cannot have three dots in any one Renown (so if your Auspex and your Tribe have the same Primary Renown, you can't put your third free dot in it as well). Since Ghost Wolves don't have a Tribe, they only get one dot in their Auspice's Primary Renown and one dot in any Renown. As per the rules for Moon Gifts, you get one Moon Gift at character creation with dots equal to your dots in your Auspice's Primary Renown. If you only have 1 dot in your Moon Gift, you also get 1 Facet of a Wolf Gift, which must be associated with a Renown you have at least one dot in. Finally, you get two free Shadow Gifts, which must both be from Gifts on your Auspice's or your Tribe's Affinity Gifts list. As per the rules for Shadow Gifts, you get one free Facet of each of these Gifts, which must be associated with a Renown you have at least one dot in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh snap, I just reread that and you are right. My Werewolf group all have one Shadow Gift Facet missing!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T00:13:41-07:00","id":943466,"title":"","content":"Thanks for all the help everyone. I think I have a better grasp on this game now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T06:30:12-07:00","id":943579,"title":"","content":"One more thing: you seemed like you were having trouble with Hunter's Aspects. The bulk of the mechanics for these are on Page 98 and the specifics for each individual aspect are found in the Conditions they inflict. Basically, in much the same way that a Vampire can Lash Out with his Predatory Aura, a Werewolf can use her Hunter's Aspect to force her aura on her prey. You roll Auspice Renown + a Power Attribute appropriate to the approach + a Skill appropriate to the situation, contested by the prey's Composure + Primal Urge. If the werewolf wins, the prey gets the Condition associated with her Auspice's Hunter's Aspect. Normally it lasts for one Scene, but on an Exceptional Success, it lasts for the werewolf's Primal Urge in days. The Conditions are found in the Appendix and explain the specific mechanics of how they affect the prey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T10:22:14-07:00","id":944393,"title":"","content":"You're not the only one confused by the rules... Hunter's Aspect and Flaring Renown can be hard to remember on top of all the gifts, merits, form rules and what-have-you. Really wish the books included a rules cheatsheet for each splatbook.<br /> <br /> Don't think I saw it mentioned so I'll add: Ghost Wolves *can* start with their 2nd dot of auspice-related renown. Like say, Purity 2 if you're Rahu. However, in addition to only having one shadow gift compared to two for a tribeswolf, they cannot start with their 2-dot Moon Gift according to Chapter One -&gt; Tribes -&gt; Ghost Wolves -&gt; Tribal Renown.<br /> <br /> The reasoning behind not having a 2nd shadow gift is that ghost wolves didn't go to tribal college. Basically, if you would have been taught in the ways of the tribe (and in the meanwhile swearing fealty to a Firstborn Rank 5-6+ demigod) either some tribal mentor teaches you a shadow gift, or teaches you to rip it from a spirit on your First Big Hunt. The reasoning behind not having access to your 2nd moon gift at creation (even if you choose to take the 2nd dot of your auspice renown) is I suppose is that by not running with a tribe, you never properly swore the Oath of the Moon, aka a Code of Honor of sorts (and fealty to the crazy godlike Rank 7+ Luna spirit)<br /> <br /> Interestingly enough the book doesn't say anything about your Moon Gift progression being stopped in-game by being a Ghost Wolf. So I guess Luna turns her head the other way regarding caring about fealty to the Oath as long as you're not a new wolf and do appropriately badass things. (Mechanically, if optimizing, this means you should *not* take your 2nd auspice renown point at chargen nor pick your free shadow-gift to be the same as your auspice... and instead acquire them in-game; this nets 2 extra exp, the cost of acquiring your 2nd dot moon gift in-game)<br /> <br /> My experience in playing a Ghost Wolf is that you will feel very limited in advancing throughout a campaign. Not counting Moon gifts, a Ghost Wolf only has easy access (3 exp unlock) to 2 gift categories of which 1 is unlocked already, compared to 4-5 (of which probably 2 are unlocked already) for someone with a tribe. You'll only be starting off with 1 category unlocked, and there's a good chance the other category has little that you want. If you want to go outside the box, the cost of unlocking a shadow gift category is 5 exp, meaning you have a huge barrier to entry. In other words, you will not feel very versatile due to exp costs... I'd suggest picking 1-2 things to be good at and sticking to it! Ghost Wolves make for very poor jack-of-all-trades, at least as far as Gifts go.<br /> <br /> The above advice does not apply if you are playing a high-exp or high-frequency campaign. But if you're playing say 3 times a month and earn 2 beats a session, it will take you about 3, 3.5 months of RL time just to unlock a non-gift category (25 beats) You could also give in and join a tribe in-game, which I bet would be a very fun RP experience.<br /> <br /> I would suggest you convince your Storyteller to be generous and take a page out of 1st Edition's The Rage handbook, giving Ghost Wolves a minor benefit -&gt; Pick *one* of the following (1) a bonus dot in non-werewolf social merits, like Allies or Contacts, to represent closer ties to humanity or even spirits, (2) if faced with a spirit enemy and he's not sure who to attack, he'd attack you last because you're &quot;unaligned&quot; and thus probably less of a Spirit Cop than a tribesman, (3) cheaper skills... this is inapplicable in 2nd edition, but if your GM is really generous, maybe you could get a free skill dot, or (4) reduce your Primal Urge penalty when talking to humans. This is completely inapplicable in 2nd edition since you don't get Primal Urge penalties, but maybe your GM would let you get a +1 to social interactions when talking to humans to show you spent more time with them.<br /> <br /> My favorite part of playing a Ghost Wolf is that my character gets to call both Forsaken and Pure the &quot;chained lapdogs of the Firstborn.&quot; Bonus points if you unlock Unchained, grow a totally unironic pink mohawk, and list &quot;The Warriors&quot; as your favorite movie. Happy gaming!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11106-captain-shoe","name":"Captain Shoe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T10:30:53-07:00","id":944399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Captain Shoe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/943174-i-don-t-get-werewolf-the-forsaken?p=944393#post944393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're not the only one confused by the rules... Hunter's Aspect and Flaring Renown can be hard to remember on top of all the gifts, merits, form rules and what-have-you. Really wish the books included a rules cheatsheet for each splatbook.<br /> <br /> Don't think I saw it mentioned so I'll add: Ghost Wolves *can* start with their 2nd dot of auspice-related renown. Like say, Purity 2 if you're Rahu. However, in addition to only having one shadow gift compared to two for a tribeswolf, they cannot start with their 2-dot Moon Gift according to Chapter One -&gt; Tribes -&gt; Ghost Wolves -&gt; Tribal Renown.<br /> <br /> The reasoning behind not having a 2nd shadow gift is that ghost wolves didn't go to tribal college. Basica